{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_f11445d10e9791e1cdc393cd7c775a514f0c026610941ac204cd9820d71f0f05", "title": "Port River", "text": "The Port River (officially known as the Port Adelaide River) is a river located north of the Adelaide central business district in the Australian state of South Australia.", "score": 17.9889}, {"id": "hp_doc_ed7f725415730405fb0c1296fb1f485a04b9447227c3f7a78b955c86b5f381cc", "title": "Torrens Island", "text": "Torrens Island is an island in the Australian state of South Australia located in the Port River Estuary between the Port River and Barker Inlet, about 15 km northwest of the state capital of Adelaide. Since European settlement of Adelaide in 1836, it has been used for a number of purposes.", "score": 14.5727}, {"id": "hp_doc_64a112efaf907fd0c20a0fb98838d8bcc5370c29b4cd3a51cdc7b6efa1580ead", "title": "Birkenhead, South Australia", "text": "Birkenhead is a north-western suburb of Adelaide 14 km from the CBD, on the Lefevre Peninsula, in the state of South Australia, Australia, and lies within the City of Port Adelaide Enfield. It is adjacent to Peterhead, Exeter and Glanville. It is bounded to the south by the Gawler Reach of the Port River, to the north by Hargrave Street and in the west and east by the Outer Harbor railway line and the Port River respectively.", "score": 14.2757}], "remaining_searches": 1}
